  "question": {
    "text": "A point source is placed at coordinates (0,1) in $x y$ -plane. A ray of light from the source is reflected on a plane mirror placed along the\r\n$X$ -axis and perpendicular to the $x y$ -plane. The reflected ray passes through the point $(3,3) .$ What is the path length of the ray from (0,1) to (3,3)$?$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "W0pQh",
      "text": "5",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
